  "slug": "curation-bioinformatics-tools-213b",
  "summary": "Preprints now map specific inference schemes onto cortical circuits, with a published method inferring interpretable decision-making agents from behavior.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is probabilistic inference as a framework for neural computation, pursued through explicit mappings to circuit-level mechanisms. A Recursive Gaussian Process formulation is mapped onto cortical microcircuits and free-energy minimization, while a recurrent Forward-Forward variant with an inverted objective is described as yielding predictive, cortex-like representations from local learning rules. A computational re-implementation of Shirazi's Bayes-Markov MAP model of V1 orientation selectivity adds quantitative evaluation via parameter sweeps, LGN noise tests, and OSI assessment. A separate published method infers minimal interpretable recurrent agent models from behavioral data, extending the same modeling logic to decision-making. What is new is the linkage of specific inference schemes to concrete substrates, with the V1 study testing one such scheme quantitatively.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-08-07"
}
